  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADD Southern Africa - Advocacy for alcohol policies to reduce harm</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADD Southern Africa programme will bring about reduction in harm from alcohol use in Southern Africa and improve achievement of the SDGs, particularly Goal 3 on health, but also other goals related to gender and child rights. SAAPA will advocate for the development, adoption and implementation of evidence-based National Alcohol Policies in Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia, South Africa and Zimbabwe. National NGO alliances in these countries will be strengthened as advocacy voices.</narrative>
  </description>
